      "id": "1",
      "title": "Situation overview",
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "1a",
          "title": "Overview",
          "bullets": [
            {
              "id": "1a.1",
              "text": "An industrial fire at Kellet Point in Osmery prompted warnings for Brayle and Sunder Flats, road closures on Kellet Road, and evacuations affecting thousands of residents. Over 2,300 people were evacuated from Brayle, with additional displacements reported in Osmery. No casualties or injuries were reported in the available tweets.",
              "confidence": "confirmed",
              "tweet_ids": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "title": "Timeline",
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "2a",
          "title": "Chronological timeline",
          "bullets": [
            {
              "id": "2a.1",
              "text": "At 11:11, Fallon Coatings deployed; warnings were issued for Brayle and later expanded to include Sunder Flats. Kellet Road was closed in the Kellet Point industrial estate and Merrin Canal by 11:16. A mandatory evacuation was ordered for Brayle at 15:23, moving about 2,300 residents, with later reports indicating 48 evacuated from Brayle and displacements in Osmery by 20:21.",
